{
  "_why": "The generic stub guesses a native function's return shape from its NAME, and for O-MicrotonalSampler every one of those guesses renders a page a user never sees: getSampleMap matches /^get/ and returns null, so handleSampleMapSnapshot bails before renderGrid() and the whole 352-cell grid, the Issues disclosure and the technique-tab cell counts stay empty; getTechniqueState returns null, so the technique bar, the CC/PC trigger panel and the Trims panel all stay hidden behind their count>1 / hasCells visibility gates; and getWaveformPeaks returns null, so the loop editor can never open. Every value below is a realistic library in this plugin's own snapshot shape, so check-ui-labels measures the page a user works in rather than an empty shell. The tuning natives are the same set O-Bells needs, for the same reason: getOctaveStretch returning null throws out of loadInitialState() before the interval list, the visualisation and the scale name ever render.",
